{
  "deliverable": "MicroBiomeNet domain-generalization: transferable taxonomic features vs raw-OTU geographic-holdout baseline",
  "date": "2026-07-04",
  "diagnosis": "The 0.405 geographic-holdout macro-F1 (MicroBiomeNetV5) is trained on top-5000 RAW OTUs. EMP deblur OTUs are exact 90bp amplicon sequence variants (BIOM observation ids are literal 90-nt DNA strings). Exact ASVs are region-specific: the same environment on different continents is dominated by different ASVs of the same higher taxa, so an ASV-keyed model learns region fingerprints that do not transfer across held-out geographic regions.",
  "innovation": "Replace raw-ASV features with coarser, more transferable representations built from the REAL Greengenes taxonomy strings inside the BIOM: per-sample OTU abundances aggregated to phylum/class/order/family/genus, CLR-transformed and concatenated (+ optional genus abundance-rank features). Higher taxa are shared across continents so the environment signal generalises better. No EMPO_3/env_biome/env_feature ever used as input; no synthetic data; identical geographic k-means holdout as the baseline.",
  "split_protocol": "TRUE geographic holdout \u2014 KMeans(20 regions, seed=42) on real (lat,lon); whole regions to train/val/test; coin-flip freshwater labels excluded; zero region leakage.",
  "baseline_neural_net_raw_otu_macro_f1": 0.404814,
  "baseline_note": "MicroBiomeNetV5 (11.7M params, CLR->sparse-attn->phylo-embed->transformer) on top-5000 OTU, full EMP, from results/benchmarks/microbiomenet_geographic_holdout_full_emp.json.",
